          "code": "SUMMARIZE_SHORTAGES",
          "id": "1766442698126",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766442698128_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use `MaterialShortageDataArray` having value `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ITEM_SHORTAGES_SUMMARY.$output?.items}}`\nEach row contains data for Material, MaterialDescription, RequiredQuantity, OpenQuantity, ShortageQuantity, UnitOfMeasure\n\n- If no shortages are found\n  `No Material Shortage found in time period.`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\n\n- If shortages are found:\n  - Generate one concise, newspaper-style headline (≤ 20 words) highlighting the most critical shortage.\n  - Do not list quantities, or multiple bullets. Do not explain.\n\nDo not include any internal identifiers or extra commentary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Work Order Data from User Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772518744764"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_WORK_ORDER_DATA_FROM_USER_QUERY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770309384208",
          "id": "1766159777864",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766159777865_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract data from User Query {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and build a REST `q` Param from the extracted data to be used for searching work orders.\n\n- Only if user is asking about a specific work order or a specific criteria, build pQparam.\n- If User Query is a generic question on Item Shortages, or missing Materials, leave pQparam as empty string.\n\n-**Build pQparam**\n   - Extract parameter values to form `pQparam` (valid Oracle REST Query Language/RQL syntax).\n    - If no duration is specified, default StartDate to the past 30 days and `EndDate` to future 7 days for field `PlannedStartDate`.\n      - For BETWEEN clauses, always use parentheses (e.g., `(PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-02-09' AND '2025-02-10')`).\n      - Output dates in YYYY-MM-DD format only.\n   - CurrentDate value is {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n    - Always use precise date values from {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}, never literal placeholder CurrentDate.\n   - If `ContextOrganizationId` having value  {{$context.$variables.ContextOrganizationId}} is available, always include the OrganizationId clause  \n    `AND OrganizationId = {{$context.$variables.ContextOrganizationId}}`\n   - For shortage-related questions, never use shortage or inventory calculations in the q param—produce only what the WorkOrder REST API natively supports for filtering.\n    - Do not append any additional clause like onHandQuantity < RequiredQuantity, RequirementQuantity > IssuedQuantity ,ShortageQuantity > 0 etc\neg.\n1) Get details for work order that starts with JKJ WO 001 in OrgId 123456789\npQparam = \"WorkOrderNumber like UPPER('JKJ WO 001%25') AND OrganizationId = 123456789 AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-02-09' AND '2025-02-10')\"\n2) Get material information for work orders in last 1 week for context Org\npQparam = \"(PlannedStartDate BETWEEN 'CurrentDate -7' AND 'CurrentDate') AND OrganizationId = ContextOrganizationId\"\n3) Get item requirements for work orders for asset Fork\npQparam = \"AssetNumber like UPPER('Fork Lift') AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN 'CurrentDate - 30' AND 'CurrentDate + 7')\"\n4) Example for a complex pQparam\npQparam = \"UPPER(WorkOrderNumber) like UPPER('aBc%25') AND (AssetNumber = 'Asset_001' OR AssetNumber = 'Asset_003' ) AND WorkOrderDescription like 'ABC Wo%25' AND WorkOrderTypeCode != 'CORRECTIVE' AND WorkOrderSubTypeCode=UPPER('ora_planned') AND WorkOrderStatusCode IN ('ORA_RELEASED','ORA_UNRELEASED') AND (PlannedStartDate BETWEEN '2025-03-07' and '2026-06-24' ) AND WorkOrderOperation.OperationSequenceNumber = 10 AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationResource.ResourceCode IS NULL AND attachments.DocumentPreviewURL IS NOT NULL AND WorkOrderOperation.WorkOrderOperationMaterial.InventoryItemNumber = 'm-assy-srl-p'\"\n\nreturn pQparam"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"pQparam\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "User Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "USER_QUERY",
          "id": "1766444061376",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766444061378_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Maintenance Material Availability Agent Context\n\nThis workflow agent supports supervisors, planners, and maintenance teams by ensuring material availability for scheduled work orders. Its role is to identify material shortages at the organization and work order level — helping maintain continuity in preventive and corrective maintenance activities.\n\n#### Maintenance Management Overview\n\nMaintenance operations depend on work orders for maintaining assets, each composed of multiple operations that may require specific materials and resources. Materials may need to be sourced, substituted, or transferred to ensure timely work order execution. The organization context defines where work orders are carried out, and your responses should help prioritize and resolve material challenges, reduce downtime, and facilitate on-time maintenance completion.\n\n#### Key Terms  \n- **Work Order:** (e.g., work order number, WO, wo#) — An instruction for maintenance of an asset, including all required operations and resources.\n- **Asset:** (e.g., Asset Number, assetnum, asset#) — Any physical equipment or plant being maintained.\n- **Operation:** (operation, OP, step) — An individual task within a work order that may need specific parts and labor.\n- **Organization:** (Organization Code, Org) — The business or facility executing maintenance.\n\n---\n\n### Data Provided\n\n- **Material Shortage Data:**  \n  `{{$context.$variables.MaterialShortageDataArray}}`  \n  Each record includes: WorkOrderId, WorkOrderNumber, AssetNumber, WoStatusName, WorkCenter, TotalShortageQuantity, and shortage details(MaterialAssignment Array).\n\n- **Chat History:**  \n  `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n### Your Task\n\n- Answer the user’s query from: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` using only the supplied data and context.\n- Do **not** infer or fabricate missing data.\n\n---\n\n### Response Rules\n\n- For queries about shortages, specific assets, items, or work orders, provide matching shortages where available.\n  - Use names, codes, or descriptions only—never show internal IDs.\n  - Suggest navigation to Material Shortage by clicking work order link from additional panel for individual shortage requirement recommendation like substitute items or available transfers from other organizations or requisition creation.\n- For queries regarding actions, explain (using only the dataset evidence) whether substitutes, transfers, or requisitions are suggested for any shortages.\n- Keep summaries and explanations concise.\n- Never reference the data set, data source or technical dataset, data provided array in your answer.\n- Do not suggest further actions or next steps unless clearly supported by the supplied data and question.\n- If no relevant information is available for the user’s query, state so clearly.\n- Only respond to the user’s question from the input message.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_MAINTENANC_WORKORDERASSIGNMENTSEQUENCES",
            "functionName": "oraScmMnt_materialAssignments_shortageForDateRange",
            "name": "Get Material Shortage For Date Range"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771390021831"
          },
          "code": "GET_MATERIAL_SHORTAGE_FOR_DATE_RANGE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771390021831",
          "id": "1771389066362",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771389752774_1",
              "name": "fromPlannedStartDate",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.StartDate}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771389752775_2",
              "name": "toPlannedStartDate",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.EndDate}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771389752776_3",
              "name": "pOrganizationId",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771389752777_4",
              "name": "materialAvailableStatus",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "'ORA_P','ORA_N'"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771389752778_5",
              "name": "pLimit",
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771389752779_6",
              "name": "pOffset",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Form Material Shortage Data for Date Range",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "// result => [{ WorkOrderId, WorkOrderNumber, WorkOrderDescription, AssetNumber, WoStatusName, WorkCenter, MaterialAvailableStatus , DistinctItemShortages, TotalShortageQuantity }, ...]\n\nconst items = $context.$nodes.GET_MATERIAL_SHORTAGE_FOR_DATE_RANGE.$output?.items ?? [];\nconst arr = Array.isArray(items) ? items : [];\n\nconst byWorkOrderId = new Map();\n\nfor (const it of arr) {\n  const woId = it?.WorkOrderId;\n  const woNum = it?.WorkOrderNumber;\n  const woDesc = ((it?.WorkOrderDescription ?? '').toString().trim() || '');\n  const assetNum = it?.AssetNumber;\n  const woStatus = it?.WoStatusName;\n  const workCenter = it?.WorkCenter;\n  const materialAvailableStatus = it?.MaterialAvailableStatus;\n  if (!woId) continue;\n\n  const rec = byWorkOrderId.get(woId) || { WorkOrderId: woId, WorkOrderNumber: woNum, WorkOrderDescription : woDesc, AssetNumber: assetNum, WoStatusName: woStatus, WorkCenter: workCenter, MaterialAvailableStatus : materialAvailableStatus, DistinctItemShortages : 0, TotalShortageQuantity:0 };\n\n const materialAssignmentItems = it?.MaterialAssignment?.items;\n rec.TotalShortageQuantity = materialAssignmentItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + Number(item.ShortageQuantity || 0), 0);\n\nconst result = materialAssignmentItems.reduce(\n  (acc, item) => {\n    const qty = Number(item.ShortageQuantity || 0);\n    if (qty > 0) {\n      acc.distinctInventoryItemIds.add(item.InventoryItemId);\n    }\n    acc.sum += qty;\n    return acc;\n  },\n  { sum: 0, distinctInventoryItemIds: new Set() }\n);\n\nrec.TotalShortageQuantity = result.sum;\nrec.DistinctItemShortages = result.distinctInventoryItemIds.size;\n\n  byWorkOrderId.set(woId, rec);\n}\n\nreturn Array.from(byWorkOrderId.values());"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771392353705"
          },
          "code": "FORM_MATERIAL_SHORTAGE_DATA_FOR_DATE_RANGE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771392353705",
          "id": "1771390021831",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Shortage Data from Time Period"
